      "question": {
        ":question/id": "c8936fd6-8a44-5c8e-bc39-2557d46fb321",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 7 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 & -6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 7 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 5 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 & -6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
